<title>USA: FREE-TO-TRADE - Farmington, N.M., $90 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>FREE-TO-TRADE - Farmington, N.M., $90 mln bonds.</headline>
<text>
<p>City of Farmington, New Mexico</p>
<p>RE: $90,000,000</p>
<p>% Pollution Control Revenue</p>
<p>Refunding Bonds, 1997 Series D</p>
<p>(Public Service Company of New Mexico San Juan Project)</p>
<p>Effective at 1:00 P.M. E.S.T., Wednesday, January 29, 1997</p>
<p>all syndicate terms and price restrictions are removed</p>
<p>and the bonds will be free to trade.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>Citicorp Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. Incorporated</p>
<p>BancAmerica Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
